 "debrief": "In Polybius’s and Livy’s accounts, the Romans surrounded Capua with a double line of works. Hannibal attacked the outer line while the garrison sallied, but both were beaten off. Hannibal then marched on Rome itself, rode up to the walls near the Colline Gate, and turned away; Fulvius had brought part of the army back to Rome, but the siege was kept up. Capua surrendered, its leaders were executed and its land confiscated. The other choices are what-ifs.",
